---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Export Compliance"
  description="Export-control, sanctions and end-use expectations for enquiries and shipments of Haiyun grain-milling equipment."
  lede="International equipment projects are subject to export-control, customs and sanctions rules. This page explains the information we need and the responsibilities that remain with the buyer."
>
  <h2>1. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This page applies to enquiries, quotations, contracts, shipments and technical data relating to
    equipment supplied by {site.legalName}. It is a summary of our expectations, not a substitute
    for legal advice or the export-control rules of any particular country.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Destination and end-use review</h2>
  <p>
    Before quoting or shipping, we may ask for the destination country, final installation site,
    intended use, end user and, where relevant, the end-use certificate or import permit. We may
    decline an enquiry or shipment where the information is incomplete, inconsistent or indicates a
    prohibited destination, end use or end user.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Sanctions and restricted parties</h2>
  <p>
    We maintain controls intended to avoid dealings with persons or entities subject to applicable
    sanctions or export restrictions. Customers and intermediaries are expected to confirm that
    they, their owners, agents and ultimate consignees are not restricted parties. We may screen
    names and destinations using available sources and may request additional ownership or
    end-user information.
  </p>
  <p>
    A confirmed match or a material risk may result in a declined order, a hold, a request for
    further information or a decision not to proceed. We will explain the reason where lawful and
    practical.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Dual-use and controlled technology</h2>
  <p>
    Some grain-milling equipment, spare parts, software or technical documents may be subject to
    export-control classification in one or more jurisdictions. The classification can depend on
    the model, capacity, automation, materials, destination and end use. Do not assume that a
    product page is an export classification.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Customer responsibilities</h2>
  <p>By submitting an enquiry or order, the customer confirms that:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the destination and end-use information provided is accurate and complete;</li>
    <li>the equipment will not be used for a prohibited weapons, military or proliferation purpose;</li>
    <li>the equipment will not be diverted to a restricted destination or end user;</li>
    <li>required import permits, licences and customs documents will be obtained;</li>
    <li>the customer will cooperate with reasonable end-use or post-shipment verification requests.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Documentation</h2>
  <p>
    Shipping and customs documents may include commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading,
    certificate of origin, fumigation or wood-packaging declarations, insurance documents and, where
    applicable, end-use statements. Document requirements vary by destination; the contract or
    freight instructions define the set for each project.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Re-export and transfer</h2>
  <p>
    Re-export, transfer, repair, servicing or transfer of technical data may be subject to separate
    rules. Customers should obtain their own advice before re-exporting equipment or sharing
    controlled technical data with a third party.
  </p>

  <h2>8. No legal advice</h2>
  <p>
    This page describes our internal expectations and does not provide legal advice or a
    determination that a transaction is permitted. Export-control and sanctions rules are complex
    and change. Obtain advice from qualified counsel or your national export authority for your
    specific transaction.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Export-compliance questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    Include the destination, end user, intended use and model or project reference so we can route
    the enquiry correctly. Postal address: {site.address.full}.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
